    "Weakness 3: The Prepositional Trap ('Make a rhyme WITH'): Colleague 9 and Colleague 13 highlighted that 'make a rhyme with' tests relational pairing (whether identical words count as making a rhyme with each other). Camp C has no textual answer for why the prompt didn't say 'Which word is NOT used in end-rhyme position?'"
